h1. FGW Test Automation – CI/CD Pipeline Documentation

----

h2. 🔭 Detailed Overview

The *FGW Test Automation Pipeline* is designed with a *decoupled architecture*, where *build and execution are separated* to improve efficiency, reduce redundant builds, and enable flexible test execution.

Unlike traditional pipelines where build and execution happen together, this pipeline supports *multiple execution modes* based on:

* Trigger type (Merge / Manual / Schedule)
* Branch (Master / Feature)

This approach ensures:
* Faster execution for testing (no rebuild needed for master runs)
* Reusability of artifacts via Nexus
* Flexibility for developers to test independently on feature branches
* Controlled release artifact generation only on master merges

---

h3. 🚀 Key Design Principles

* *Decoupled Build & Run* → Build happens only during master merge
* *Artifact Reuse* → Master run downloads JAR from Nexus instead of rebuilding
* *Environment Flexibility* → Same JAR can be reused across executions
* *Controlled Deployment* → Only master branch publishes artifacts
* *Developer Independence* → Feature branches run without Nexus dependency

---

h2. ⚡ Pipeline Execution Modes

|| Trigger Type || Branch || Stages Executed || JAR Source ||
| Merge (CI Trigger) | master | preparation → build → upload | Generated & uploaded to Nexus |
| Manual / Schedule | master | run → notify | Downloaded from Nexus |
| Manual / Schedule | feature | build → run → notify | Built within pipeline |

---

h2. 🔀 Workflow Logic

Pipeline behavior depends on both *branch* and *trigger type*:

* *Merge to master*
** Executes build pipeline
** Stages: preparation → build → upload
** Publishes JAR to Nexus
** No test execution

* *Manual trigger on master*
** Executes test pipeline
** Stages: run → notify
** JAR is downloaded from Nexus

* *Manual trigger on feature branch*
** Executes full pipeline
** Stages: build → run → notify
** JAR is built within pipeline

* *Feature branch push*
** Pipeline is *not triggered*

---

h2. 🧱 Stage Definitions

|| Stage || Description || Used In ||
| preparation | Prepares environment and validates project | Master merge / Feature |
| build | Builds JAR using Maven | Master merge / Feature |
| upload | Uploads JAR to Nexus | Master merge only |
| run | Executes fgw-injector JAR | Manual pipelines |
| notify | Sends email with results | All manual runs |

