h2. 🟢 Master Pipeline

h3. 1. Merge to Master (CI Trigger)

* Executes:
** preparation → build → upload
* Generates JAR file
* Uploads artifact to Nexus repository
* Does NOT execute tests

---

h3. 2. Manual / Scheduled Run (Master)

* Executes:
** run → notify
* Downloads JAR from Nexus
* Executes test workflows using fgw-injector
* Sends email notification

---

h2. 🔵 Feature Pipeline

Feature pipelines are used for *development-level testing*.

* Executes:
** build → run → notify
* JAR is built inside pipeline
* No interaction with Nexus
* Faster for iterative testing

---

h2. 📧 Notification Logic

Email notifications are sent after pipeline execution.

|| Pipeline Type || Recipients || Notes ||
| Master (Manual) | DEV + TEST Team | Includes full test results |
| Feature | DEV Team Only | For development testing |

* Email subject changes based on trigger type
* Logs are attached as ZIP file

---

h2. ⚙️ Pipeline Variables

|| Variable || Description ||
| EXECUTION_MODE | Controls pipeline behavior (DEV_TRIGGER / WEB / SCHEDULE) |
| JARArgument1 | Selects test workflow (C2B, E2E, etc.) |

---

h2. 🧪 Supported Test Workflows

The pipeline supports multiple workflows via *JARArgument1*:

* C2B-Workflow
* E2E-Workflow
* B2B-Passthrough
* Negative-PSR
* SAM-Workflow
* UIValidation
* OFMT / OFMT1 / OFMT2
* ACSP-Workflow

---

h2. 📖 Run Instructions

h3. Feature Pipeline Execution

# Go to *GitLab → CI/CD → Pipelines*
# Click *Run Pipeline*
# Select feature branch
# Provide *JARArgument1*
# Click *Run*
# Monitor logs
# Check email for results

---

h3. Master Test Execution

# Go to *Run Pipeline*
# Select *master branch*
# Trigger pipeline
# JAR will be downloaded from Nexus
# Execution starts
# Email sent after completion

---

h2. ⚠️ Important Notes

* Feature branch push does NOT trigger pipeline
* JAR artifact expires (if using pipeline artifact)
* Master pipeline always uses Nexus artifact
* Build is NOT triggered during manual master execution

---

h2. ✅ Summary

* Master Merge → Build & Upload
* Master Manual → Run using Nexus JAR
* Feature → Build + Run
* Pipeline behavior is fully controlled via trigger + branch
